# Which Spark is the hub: the one Spark that runs Spark Console and Sparkie, is never powered off and never gets the
# shutdown rule (R41). Every script under deploy/ takes a Spark's address, name or number from this file and nowhere
# else (deploy/hub.sh reads it). service/config.json must say the same: the hub is its Spark with "host": "local", the
# others are at these addresses, its "user" is LOGIN and its "origin" is https://HUB_NAME.TAILNET:8443. The installer
# refuses a build where the two disagree. Moving the hub: docs/how/move-the-hub.md.
# One value a line, NAME=value, no quotes or spaces; a Spark's line is its id and its tailnet address. One line of sed
# reads any of them, for example Spark 3's address:   sed -n 's/^spark3=//p' deploy/hub.env
HUB=spark1
HUB_NAME=akspark1
LOGIN=akuppala
TAILNET=tailab9aa9.ts.net
spark1=100.119.233.101
spark2=100.79.155.126
spark3=100.122.49.9
spark4=100.109.240.15
